0Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.2\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.2\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K39AA58W1S0Q5G9/prj_1KESD32TS1S0ZHGV/pjd_1KMJYPYMN1S0REVM/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 25 Mar 2026\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KHBTGDVJ1S06DQ4?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K39AA58W1S0Q5G9/prj_1KESD32TS1S0ZHGV/pjd_1M0HNDXCT1S0708G/explanatory_note.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K39AA58W1S0Q5G9/prj_1KESD32TS1S0ZHGV/pjd_1KXR3QMH11S0FTT9/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K39AA58W1S0Q5G9/prj_1KESD32TS1S0ZHGV/pjd_1KXR3QB6K1S08H2Z/validation_and_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K39AA58W1S0Q5G9/prj_1KESD32TS1S0ZHGV/pjd_1KPZPQ3411S0MX3P/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K39AA58W1S0Q5G9/prj_1KESD32TS1S0ZHGV/pjd_1KMJYPYMN1S0REVM/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\n200Y+\\nBurney Forest Power v1.2\\nBiochar Solutions\\nISSUED\\n2,821.91\\nBUFFER POOL\\n56.439\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Jul 2023 to 01 Jul 2028\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nBurney Forest Power is a biomass power plant in Burney, California, that generates electricity and produces biochar by gasifying wood waste and forest residue using fixed grate stoker technology.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\n3YMF\\nApproval date\\n17 Jul 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.2\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nBurney Forest Power v1.2\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n25 Mar 2026\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 2,821.91 tCO₂e removed from Burney Forest Power v1.2 on 31 Dec 2023\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n2,821.906 t\\nSequestrations\\n3,026.515 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n188.560 tCO₂e\\n-\\nUncertainty Discount\\n16.049 t\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nIndustry by-products (Walnut shells) v1.2\\tBiomass\\t17 Jul 2026\\nMill hog fuel v1.2\\tBiomass\\t17 Jul 2026\\nWood residues v1.2\\tBiomass\\t17 Jul 2026\\nShowing 3 of 3\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n21 Aug 2026\\tExplanatory Note\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Jul 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Jul 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n24 Apr 2026\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n25 Mar 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 5\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n2,821.91\\nRetired\\n0\\nBuffer pool\\n56.439\\nCrediting period\\n01 Jul 2023 to 01 Jul 2028\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n17 Jul 2026\\t2,821.91\\t56.439\\t2,765.471\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Biochar Solutions's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 56.439 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 56.439 certificates.\\n\\nBiochar Solutions has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"